#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:90
msgid "Key design principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:92
msgid "**Run as the user (or as the agent user)** — no ``sudo`` on business data. Odoo ACLs and record rules always apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:94
msgid "**AI policy narrows, with one named exception** — ``ai.access.rule`` can never grant a right the underlying user does not already hold in Odoo. Within that ceiling, a rule naming a specific **field** is the one place a rule *opens* something the gate otherwise refuses: a field that also writes into another model. A model-level Allow deliberately never lifts that — see :ref:`ai/policy/cross-model`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:100
msgid "**Capabilities are master switches** — e.g. Write / Delete / Web / MCP / Customize ship disabled until an admin turns them on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:102
msgid "**Default-deny channels for agents** — an agent without a matching channel rule refuses inbound address (Discuss DM, @mention, activity, assignment)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:104
msgid "**Supervisor four-eyes by default on agent writes** — each agent **task** has its own :guilabel:`Write Mode` (default **Always require confirmation**). Unattended runs therefore propose for the supervisor unless that task explicitly opts into *hybrid* or *auto* for trusted, low-risk work (for example filling **draft** vendor bills that the playbook never posts). The global chat write mode does **not** control agent runs — see :ref:`ai/agents/task-write-mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:111
msgid "**Customer / email text is work material, not authority** — instructions in a ticket body cannot raise the agent's privileges; triage and capability ceilings subtract only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:114
msgid "**Grounding** — the assistant must not invent models, fields or stages; it uses tools and live environment facts for *this* database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:116
msgid "**Runs are accounted for** — cancellation is cooperative and recorded, never a silent kill: the run stops at its next step boundary and closes as failed with a cancellation reason. A run whose worker died is closed by a scheduled housekeeping job, which rebuilds its ledger row from the dispatch record where one survives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:121
msgid "**A structural refusal is not abuse** — the gate refuses plenty the model merely guessed at (a non-writable field, a field that also writes another model) without recording a violation or spending a strike, so an empty Violations list is not proof that nothing was refused. Strikes are for real boundaries: a secret or privileged field, an explicit policy Deny, a disabled capability."
msgstr ""

