#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:20
msgid ":guilabel:`User`: can open the Documents app, and work with the files they have access to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:21
msgid ":guilabel:`Manager`: can additionally configure folders, tags, and operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:24
msgid "Browse documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:26
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Documents --> Documents` to list the files of the database. The list, kanban, and form views show, for each document, its :guilabel:`Folder`, :guilabel:`Tags`, the related :guilabel:`Partner` and :guilabel:`Model`, and the file :guilabel:`Type`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:30
msgid "The search panel and the search view help narrow the list down:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:32
msgid "group the documents by :guilabel:`Folder`, :guilabel:`Model`, :guilabel:`Partner`, :guilabel:`Tag`, or :guilabel:`Type`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:34
msgid "use the :guilabel:`Hide JS/CSS`, :guilabel:`Hide View Model`, and :guilabel:`Hide Without Model` filters to leave out the technical attachments that Odoo stores together with the business files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:37
msgid "Each document has a chatter, so notes and activities can be logged on a file itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:47
msgid "Download several documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:49
msgid "To download several documents at once, select them in the list view, click the :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`Actions` button, and select :guilabel:`Download Files`. Odoo proposes a file name for the archive (`files_<date>.zip`); confirm with :guilabel:`Download Files` to get all selected documents in a single ZIP file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:55
msgid "The file name must end with `.zip`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:58
msgid "Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:60
msgid "Folders classify documents and can be nested. To create one, go to :menuselection:`Documents --> Configuration --> Folders` and click :guilabel:`New`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:63
msgid ":guilabel:`Folder Name` and :guilabel:`Parent Folder`: the position of the folder in the tree. The :guilabel:`Complete Name` of a folder shows its full path, e.g. `Contracts / 2026`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:65
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: leave empty to make the folder available to all companies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:66
msgid ":guilabel:`Sequence`: the order of the folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:68
msgid "The :guilabel:`Documents` smart button opens the documents filed in the folder, and the :guilabel:`Child Folders` tab lists its subfolders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:72
msgid "Automatic folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:74
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Automatic Folder` section, an :guilabel:`Auto Model` can be selected. Documents attached to a record of that model are then filed automatically in the folder, without the user having to select it. Subfolders of an automatic folder inherit this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:89
msgid "Tags describe the content of a document. They are grouped into **tag categories**, and both the categories and the tags can be attached to a folder, so that only the relevant tags are proposed on a document of that folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:93
msgid "To manage them, go to :menuselection:`Documents --> Configuration --> Tags`. Create a category, give it a :guilabel:`Folder` if it should only apply there, and add the :guilabel:`Tags` with their :guilabel:`Color`. A tag name must be unique within its category, and a category name must be unique within its folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:99
msgid "Share a document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:101
msgid "Open a document and, in the :guilabel:`Share` section of the form, click :guilabel:`Share File`. Odoo generates a share :guilabel:`URL` that can be copied with the :icon:`fa-clipboard` :guilabel:`(copy)` icon and sent to anyone: the link gives access to the file without logging in. Click :guilabel:`Unshare File` to invalidate the link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:106
msgid "Both actions are logged in the document's chatter, with the user and the date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:117
msgid "Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:119
msgid "An **operation** turns a document into a record, or links it to an existing one — for example, to register a vendor bill from a received PDF, or to attach a signed contract to a project task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:122
msgid "To define an operation, go to :menuselection:`Documents --> Configuration --> Operations` and click :guilabel:`New`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:125
msgid ":guilabel:`Operation Name`: the name proposed to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:126
msgid ":guilabel:`Folders` and :guilabel:`Models`: restrict the operation to documents in specific folders or attached to specific models. Leave empty to apply it everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/documents.rst:128
msgid ":guilabel:`Operation`: :guilabel:`Creating a New Record` or :guilabel:`Link to an Existing Record`."
