#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:983
msgid "Access control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:985
msgid "Control who can create, edit, and use templates:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:987
msgid "**eYssen Sign User**: can use templates to create and send signing requests, and can view their own requests and the requests where they are a signer or a follower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:989
msgid "**eYssen Sign Manager**: full access to all templates, requests, and configuration, including roles, field types, workflows, webhooks, and settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:997
msgid "eYssen Sign implements multiple layers of security:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:999
msgid "**Role-based access**: the *eYssen Sign User* and *eYssen Sign Manager* groups control access levels. Users can only see requests they created, are assigned to sign, or are following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1001
msgid "**Record rules**: enforce row-level security so users cannot access requests belonging to others unless they are a participant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1003
msgid "**Rate limiting**: the shared signing endpoint implements rate limiting to prevent abuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1004
msgid "**SSRF protection**: webhook URLs are validated to block requests to private or internal network addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1006
msgid "**XSS protection**: chatter messages and user-supplied content are sanitized to prevent cross-site scripting attacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1008
msgid "**State machine enforcement**: terminal states (*Signed*, *Refused*, *Canceled*, *Expired*) cannot be reversed, preventing unauthorized state manipulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1014
msgid "Digitally signed PDF reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1016
msgid "The *E-Sign* (``eyssen_esign``) module is a separate feature: instead of collecting handwritten signatures, it applies a **digital signature** to the PDF files Odoo generates, so that the recipient can verify that the document was issued by the company and has not been altered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1020
msgid "To enable it for a report, activate the :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Reports`, open the report (e.g., the customer invoice), and enable :guilabel:`E-sign report`. From then on, every PDF generated from that report is signed before it is downloaded, printed, or sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:1026
msgid "The signature is applied by the eYssen signing service, so the database must be able to reach it. Each signed report is recorded in the technical logs."
msgstr ""

